===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*solh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|solidus}}, from classical {{der|en|la|solidus||[[solid]]}}, see below. {{doublet|en|sol|sold|soldo|solid|sou|xu}}.

In [[numismatic]] and weight senses, via medieval {{der|en|la|solidus||[[various]] [[coin]]s}}, from  {{der|en|LL.|solidus||a [[gold coin]] of the [[Roman Empire]]}}. In chemical sense, via {{der|en|de|Solidus}}, coined by [[w:H.W.B. Roozeboom|H.W.B. Roozeboom]] in his 1899 ''Zeitschrift für Physikalische Chemie, Stöchiometrie, und Verwandtschaftslehre'' (XXX, page 387).

In [[typography]], from the [[shilling mark]] originally being an abbreviation (a [[long s]] ⟨{{m|mul|ſ}}⟩), of Medieval Latin ''solidus'' meaning {{m|en|shilling}}.

